1
00:00:03,688 --> 00:00:05,069
This is ScholarCrew

2
00:00:05,069 --> 00:00:10,738
a crew of AI specialists that helps a high school student get into college and

3
00:00:10,738 --> 00:00:11,538
pay for it.

4
00:00:11,538 --> 00:00:15,245
Every week starts here: the next step, a short plan

5
00:00:15,245 --> 00:00:17,280
and the deadlines coming up.

6
00:00:17,282 --> 00:00:19,249
Ledger, the money specialist

7
00:00:19,249 --> 00:00:24,729
shows what Jordan's top school will really cost: the gap between the price and

8
00:00:24,729 --> 00:00:25,502
free money.

9
00:00:25,502 --> 00:00:28,101
It's calculated by code, not guessed.

10
00:00:28,103 --> 00:00:28,637
In Crew

11
00:00:28,637 --> 00:00:34,125
Jordan asks a question and Compass coordinates the specialists it needs.

12
00:00:34,125 --> 00:00:38,623
Every answer shows what the team used, with verified dates.

13
00:00:38,626 --> 00:00:40,239
Asking takes seconds.

14
00:00:40,239 --> 00:00:44,004
The answer is a short plan with one-click actions

15
00:00:44,004 --> 00:00:47,077
and nothing changes until Jordan clicks.

16
00:00:50,025 --> 00:00:52,846
Scout matches scholarships rule by rule

17
00:00:52,846 --> 00:00:58,198
ranks them by dollars per hour of effort, and hides scams with the reason.

18
00:00:59,394 --> 00:01:03,662
Every listing shows each rule next to Jordan's matching fact

19
00:01:03,662 --> 00:01:06,863
with the source and the date it was verified.

20
00:01:06,864 --> 00:01:10,421
In Essay Studio, Quill coaches but never writes.

21
00:01:10,421 --> 00:01:15,016
Each comment quotes Jordan's own sentence and asks a question.

22
00:01:16,026 --> 00:01:20,669
The Story Bank keeps each of Jordan's moments in their own words.

23
00:01:20,669 --> 00:01:26,311
Quill matches stories to new prompts, so one good story can answer many essays.

24
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:32,368
Atlas keeps the college list balanced, with each school's deadline, checklist

25
00:01:32,368 --> 00:01:34,457
and yearly gap side by side.

26
00:01:35,324 --> 00:01:38,823
When award letters arrive, Aid reads every line

27
00:01:38,823 --> 00:01:42,470
and Ledger compares what each school really costs

28
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:44,927
for year one and over four years.

29
00:01:44,928 --> 00:01:47,524
Prep turns test scores into dollars.

30
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:53,077
It computes the superscore and shows whether a retake would unlock more merit

31
00:01:53,077 --> 00:01:54,808
aid at Jordan's schools.

32
00:01:54,809 --> 00:02:00,379
Impact tracks service hours that supervisors confirm with a single email link

33
00:02:00,379 --> 00:02:05,009
and shows how close Jordan is to each scholarship's requirement.

34
00:02:05,012 --> 00:02:10,220
Parents can help, but students decide what's shared, one category at a time.

35
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,484
For recommendation letters

36
00:02:15,484 --> 00:02:21,465
Jordan sends teachers a read-only helper link: a brag sheet that expires and can

37
00:02:21,465 --> 00:02:23,185
be revoked at any time.

38
00:02:23,188 --> 00:02:27,603
And everything the crew remembers is visible, with its source

39
00:02:27,603 --> 00:02:29,847
and can be edited or forgotten.

40
00:02:31,340 --> 00:02:33,448
ScholarCrew is free to start.

41
00:02:33,448 --> 00:02:39,338
The Family plan covers a student and up to two parents for twelve dollars a month

42
00:02:39,338 --> 00:02:42,973
or there's a season pass for seventy-nine dollars.

43
00:02:42,973 --> 00:02:48,644
Prices are still being tested, and paying never unlocks anyone's private data.

44
00:02:48,648 --> 00:02:49,499
ScholarCrew.

45
00:02:49,499 --> 00:02:51,840
One plan to get in and pay for it

46
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:56,096
with a crew that never writes your essay or sells your data.
